Subject: Keep Safari video playback background black

Safari can show white browser chrome when the page background is transparent
and the video controls fade out. Keep the document background black only while
the HTML video player exists; native players still need document transparency.
Verified with a live-container override on iPhone Safari.

Diff stays in the accepted queue so stable and nightly reconstructions retain it.

diff --git a/src/index.html b/src/index.html
--- a/src/index.html
+++ b/src/index.html
@@ -29,6 +29,11 @@
             background-color: transparent !important;
         }
 
+        /* Safari needs an opaque page background after video controls fade. */
+        html.transparentDocument:has(.videoPlayerContainer) {
+            background: #000 !important;
+        }
+
         .layout-tv .mouseIdle,
         .layout-tv .mouseIdle button,
         .layout-tv .mouseIdle select,
